Package: @PACKAGE@
Name: @NAME@
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: iphoneos-arm
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Author: @AUTHOR@
Section: Keyboards
Priority: optional
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Recommends: @RECOMMENDS@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Homepage: @HOMEPAGE@
Description: Unicode @EMOJI_VERSION@ emoji in the iOS 6 emoji keyboard
 The iOS 6 emoji palette is not a plist. It is six hard-coded UTF-16 string
 constants compiled into UIKit, so replacing the emoji font makes modern emoji
 drawable but leaves the keyboard offering the same @STOCK_COUNT@ characters
 it shipped with in 2012.
 .
 This package hooks +[UIKeyboardEmojiCategory categoryForType:] and appends
 the rest of Unicode Emoji @EMOJI_VERSION@ to the five fixed categories:
 Smileys and People go to People, animals and plants to Nature, food,
 activities and objects to Objects, travel and flags to Places, and the
 remaining symbols to Symbols. The palette has exactly six category slots
 wired into UIKit's artwork and layout, so no seventh tab is added.
 .
 This needs a font that can draw those emoji, which is why it depends on
 @FONTPACKAGE@ (>= @EMOJI_VERSION@) — the two are built from the same
 Unicode emoji-test.txt and are meant to be installed together. It is also
 belt and braces: every candidate is offered to CoreText before it is added,
 single scalars through CTFontGetGlyphsForCharacters and multi-scalar
 sequences through a CTLine that has to collapse to exactly one glyph in the
 emoji font itself. Anything the installed font cannot draw as one glyph is
 dropped, so the grid never shows a tofu box or half of a family. On the
 stock Apple 2012 font almost nothing passes that test and the keyboard
 stays as it was, which is the correct outcome rather than a failure.
 .
 The candidate list is @CANDIDATES@ sequences generated from the same
 Unicode emoji-test.txt the font is built from. Shaping runs once at install
 time and the resulting glyph ids are cached, so opening the keyboard costs
 a few milliseconds rather than a few seconds.
 .
 If a hooked class or selector is not the shape this build expects, the tweak
 installs nothing at all and the keyboard behaves exactly as it does without
 the package. Creating /var/lib/emojikeyboard/disabled switches it off
 without uninstalling.
